      "text": "Post-Stall Navigation with Fixed-Wing UAVs using Onboard Vision",
      "bbox": [
        70.96299743652344,
        74.0442886352539,
        541.0394287109375,
        88.3745346069336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Adam Polevoy1, Max Basescu1, Luca Scheuer1, Joseph Moore1",
      "bbox": [
        157.98800659179688,
        106.934814453125,
        445.8401184082031,
        118.79217529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract— Recent research has enabled ﬁxed-wing unmanned",
      "bbox": [
        63.9630126953125,
        151.4922637939453,
        298.8008728027344,
        159.5530548095703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "aerial vehicles (UAVs) to maneuver in constrained spaces",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        161.45423889160156,
        298.8006591796875,
        169.51502990722656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "through the use of direct nonlinear model predictive control",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        171.41725158691406,
        298.8006286621094,
        179.47804260253906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(NMPC) [1]. However, this approach has been limited to a",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        181.38026428222656,
        298.80059814453125,
        189.44105529785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "priori known maps and ground truth state measurements. In",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        191.3422393798828,
        298.8006286621094,
        199.4030303955078
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this paper, we present a direct NMPC approach that leverages",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        201.3052520751953,
        298.8006591796875,
        209.3660430908203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "NanoMap [2], a light-weight point-cloud mapping framework to",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        211.2682647705078,
        298.8006591796875,
        219.3290557861328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generate collision-free trajectories using onboard stereo vision.",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        221.23023986816406,
        298.80059814453125,
        229.29103088378906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We ﬁrst explore our approach in simulation and demonstrate",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        231.19325256347656,
        298.8006896972656,
        239.25404357910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that our algorithm is sufﬁcient to enable vision-based navigation",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        241.15626525878906,
        298.8006896972656,
        249.21705627441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in urban environments. We then demonstrate our approach in",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        251.1182403564453,
        298.80072021484375,
        259.17901611328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hardware using a 42-inch ﬁxed-wing UAV and show that our",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        261.08123779296875,
        298.8006896972656,
        269.14202880859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "motion planning algorithm is capable of navigating around a",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        271.043212890625,
        298.8006591796875,
        279.10400390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "building using a minimalistic set of goal-points. We also show",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        281.0062255859375,
        298.8006591796875,
        289.0670166015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that storing a point-cloud history is important for navigating",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        290.96923828125,
        298.80059814453125,
        299.030029296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these types of constrained environments.",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001525878906,
        300.9312438964844,
        213.11776733398438,
        308.9920654296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "I. INTRODUCTION",
      "bbox": [
        137.52601623535156,
        319.2164306640625,
        215.27880859375,
        328.12298583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rotary-wing unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are often",
      "bbox": [
        63.96302032470703,
        334.4314270019531,
        298.8014221191406,
        343.3379821777344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "preferred for navigating in constrained environments. Not",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        346.38641357421875,
        298.8009948730469,
        355.29296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "only are they capable of near zero turn radii, but many",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        358.3424072265625,
        298.8010559082031,
        367.24896240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "are amendable to differentially ﬂat representations that can",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        370.2973937988281,
        298.80108642578125,
        379.2039489746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "greatly reduce computational requirements for online trajec-",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        382.25238037109375,
        298.80096435546875,
        391.158935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tory optimization [3]. By contrast, ﬁxed-wing UAVs offer",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        394.2073669433594,
        298.80096435546875,
        403.1139221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "signiﬁcant advantages over rotary-wing UAVs in terms of",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        406.162353515625,
        298.801025390625,
        415.06890869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "energy efﬁciency, endurance, and speed. Traditionally ﬁxed-",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        418.1173400878906,
        298.80096435546875,
        427.0238952636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "wing UAVs have been hindered by limited maneuverability",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        430.0733337402344,
        298.8009948730469,
        438.9798889160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and restricted to large open spaces. Recent research has",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        442.0283203125,
        298.8010559082031,
        450.93487548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "shown that aerobatic ﬁxed-wing UAVs are capable of navi-",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        453.9833068847656,
        298.8009948730469,
        462.8898620605469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gating through complex environments by exploiting the full",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        465.93829345703125,
        298.8009338378906,
        474.8448486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬂight envelope [4], [1]. By operating beyond the conventional",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        477.8932800292969,
        298.8009338378906,
        486.7998352050781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬂight regimes, there is an opportunity to achieve both range",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        489.8492736816406,
        298.8009948730469,
        498.7558288574219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and maneuverability in a single vehicle.",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        501.80426025390625,
        217.50619506835938,
        510.7108154296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In [1], the authors demonstrated that a ﬁxed-wing UAV",
      "bbox": [
        63.96302032470703,
        513.779296875,
        298.8013916015625,
        522.6858520507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "could navigate a narrow corridor by executing post-stall",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        525.7342529296875,
        298.8009338378906,
        534.6408081054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "turns via nonlinear model predictive control (NMPC). While",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        537.6902465820312,
        298.8009948730469,
        546.5968017578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this approach proved a promising means to increase ﬁxed-",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        549.645263671875,
        298.8010559082031,
        558.5518188476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "wing maneuverability, it required an a priori map of the",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        561.6002197265625,
        298.801025390625,
        570.5067749023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "environment. For real-world applications, full a priori map",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        573.5552368164062,
        298.801025390625,
        582.4617919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "information is often not practical. Rather, the vehicle must",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        585.51025390625,
        298.8009948730469,
        594.4168090820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "navigate in an unknown environment and construct a map",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        597.4652709960938,
        298.80096435546875,
        606.371826171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "during runtime for collision avoidance and navigation.",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        609.4212646484375,
        276.5445251464844,
        618.3278198242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Real-time mapping poses a number of signiﬁcant chal-",
      "bbox": [
        63.96302032470703,
        621.396240234375,
        298.8013916015625,
        630.3027954101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lenges, for aerobatic, fast-moving ﬁxed-wing UAVs. Slower-",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        633.3512573242188,
        298.8009948730469,
        642.2578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "moving multi-rotor UAVs have long relied on sensors that",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        645.3062744140625,
        298.80096435546875,
        654.2128295898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "leverage LIDAR (e.g.,[5]). However, these sensors are often",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        657.2622680664062,
        298.80096435546875,
        666.1688232421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "too heavy for small aerobatic ﬁxed-wings, have update rates",
      "bbox": [
        54.00001907348633,
        669.21728515625,
        298.801025390625,
        678.1238403320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
